{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"body":"Final rebar-debug report for 2bd6-ff87-d48c-4a65 / unsavoury-desertic-ant.\n\nProblem: Anthropic 1.x/httpx2 rejects rebar's retrying Anthropic seam because the seam passed a stdlib `httpx.AsyncClient`.\n\nProven root cause: `src/rebar/llm/anthropic_model.py:_build_retrying_anthropic_provider` was hard-coded to stdlib httpx client/transport/exception types. Under `anthropic==1.2.0`, `AsyncAnthropic.__init__` requires `httpx2.AsyncClient`, producing `TypeError: Expected an instance of httpx2.AsyncClient but got <class 'httpx.AsyncClient'>`. The fix is at `src/rebar/llm/anthropic_model.py:107-117,133-178,185-212,299-340`.\n\nProof: reproduced the exact TypeError against `anthropic==1.2.0`; signature inspection showed 1.2.0 annotation `httpx2.AsyncClient | None` and 0.121.0 annotation `httpx.AsyncClient | None`. Anthropic 1.2.0 beta `messages.create` also drops `temperature`, `top_p`, `top_k` but accepts `extra_body`. MockTransport experiments proved httpx2 client construction, retry, and sampling-through-extra_body work.\n\nDefect origin: caused_by recorded to `morbid-uncultured-arcticduck` / `95a5-41eb-cffd-477b`, commit `434dc0a5779f164a082cd688783d71024fd93837`, which introduced the custom stdlib-httpx transport-owned retry seam. 1f35 was only the stopgap cap; 254e hardened the same seam but did not create the upstream httpx2 obligation.\n\nTests: RED/GREEN coverage in `tests/unit/test_transport_retry.py:243-310`; provider-parity and harness compatibility coverage in `tests/unit/test_provider_parity.py`, `test_llm_fallback_chain.py`, `test_agentic_message_cache.py`, `test_llm_provider_factory.py`, `test_llm_timeouts.py`, `test_cache_prefix_breakpoint.py`, `test_candidate_tracing.py`, `test_candidate_tracing_oracle.py`, and `test_llm_config_gate_root.py`; dependency contract in `tests/unit/test_packaging_dependencies.py`. The RED oracle failed before the seam fix and passed after. Sandboxed mutation reintroduced stdlib-httpx / sampling-drop defects and returned the targeted tests to RED.\n\nFix: select the SDK's expected HTTP module from the `AsyncAnthropic` signature; build stdlib httpx for pre-1 SDKs and httpx2 for 1.x; share RetryConfig/wait/validate logic; add an httpx2 tenacity transport fallback; coerce timeouts; move unsupported real sampling kwargs to `extra_body`; widen `anthropic` to `>=0.121.0,<2`.\n\nScope & safety: caller sweep found production `ProviderSession._build_anthropic` plus direct helper tests; all affected MockTransport harnesses were updated. The fix restores approved Decision-6 compatibility, adds no new dependency, and weakens no tests.\n\nSiblings: construct sweep found no other production Anthropic custom-client seams; test harness siblings listed above were fixed. Parity sweep: ProviderSession remains the single production channel for Anthropic provider construction; no missing CLI/MCP/library surface.\n\nResidual risk & prevention: pydantic-ai's future first-party `HTTPX2TenacityTransport` is handled opportunistically if present; pinned version lacks it. Private pydantic-ai dispatch through `client.beta.messages.create` is guarded by a spy test so a future refactor fails loudly. No undispositioned fragility remains.\n\nReplication: merged Gerrit change 2470 as commit `90957179ed7b9a290ebefec5ff77d76945385834`; LLM-Review +1 and Verified +1. Post-merge local replication on origin/main: targeted httpx2/provider-parity tests passed (5 passed), and `rebar verify-commit-ticket --rev HEAD` resolved this ticket."},"env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","event_type":"COMMENT","timestamp":1788241374437320001,"uuid":"313fd5ed-6983-4bf7-ae92-e269210d63a4"}